+  # PATCH (CLAUDE.md): the transaction FSM uses get_in(data, [:trans, :last_response])
+  # / get_in(state, [:data, :transaction, :last_response]) (transaction_statem.ex),
+  # which calls Access on this struct. Structs don't implement Access by default →
+  # (UndefinedFunctionError) Transaction.fetch/2. Implement Access (delegating to
+  # Map) so those get_in traversals work, unblocking 200 OK handling on real calls.
+  @behaviour Access
+  @impl Access
+  def fetch(struct, key), do: Map.fetch(struct, key)
+  @impl Access
+  def get_and_update(struct, key, fun), do: Map.get_and_update(struct, key, fun)
+  @impl Access
+  def pop(struct, key), do: Map.pop(struct, key)
